      "lineNbr": 645,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-31T06:41:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s handled above is something like when roaming from BSSID A1 of network A to BSSID A2 of the same network A. We now completely rely on firmware to initiate this kind of switching if the feature is supported. \n\nThe case here is when we switch from network A to network B, different SSID. Firmware doesn\u0027t initiate this kind of transition. It\u0027s up to the framework to trigger it. In addition to SSID, we used to specify BSSID as well. Now only SSID is specified and we let firmware to choose which BSSID to connect to.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 645,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 645,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "21f7c746784993d3002f9a2da59575a70544ecfa",
