    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52a89a72_b9a1be13",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4027,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-31T00:01:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "when explicitly asked for the feature set (syncGetSupportedFeatureSet) we do not return a copy of the returned value.  Is there a reason we do not do that?  (In other words, is this ok to cache? Should this be retrieved each time?)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4027,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4027,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "21f7c746784993d3002f9a2da59575a70544ecfa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "13ee977b_ec1af18c",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4027,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-31T06:41:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "syncGetSupportedFeatures() masks out the RTT bits depending on the system property settings. Here all we care about is the WIFI_FEATURE_CONTROL_ROAMING bit. This feature is fixed with the version of SoC and firmware. It doesn\u0027t change on the fly. So it\u0027s okay to cache. We need to check this flag for every network switching, which can happen every 10 seconds in theory. Retrieving it every single time via HAL, driver and firmware can become very expensive. syncGetSupportedFeatures() is not called that often.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4027,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4027,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "21f7c746784993d3002f9a2da59575a70544ecfa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5360164d_58098ff9",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4027,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-01T05:59:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it is only set once based on system properties, then do we need to grab it every time we reload firmware or can it be done once at boot?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4027,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4027,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "21f7c746784993d3002f9a2da59575a70544ecfa",
